WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.030
If you want to hear my theory about what Chucky’s
original plan may have been and how it was

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.560
altered in desperation, then stick around
to the end of this video.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.180
Welcome back to Things You Missed, the show
where I find the most thoughtful and intelligent

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.439
analysis and discussion about horror cinema,
except we’re covering a movie about a dumb

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:23.699
kid and a killer doll who at one point blows
up a house, so let’s just throw all that

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:27.730
intelligent analysis stuff out the window
with Aunt Maggie and get into the Things You

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:28.240
Missed.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.500
The movie begins in Chicago, where serial
killer Charles Lee Ray is fleeing from the

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.500
police.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.430
I heard online somewhere that the name Charles
Lee Ray comes from combining the names of

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.910
serial killer Charles Manson, and assassins
Lee Harvey Oswald and James Earl Ray, and

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.910
I only wish that he would have actually succeeding
in taking over Andy Barclay’s body, because

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.920
that would have may him Charles Barkley.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.070
Apparently before Jimmy Wong was on Feasts
of Fiction, he also ran his own Cantonese

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.750
restaurant, outside of which Charles Lee Ray
gets shot.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.080
Anyone find it a little strange that he bleeds
more in his doll form than he does as a human?

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Anyways, he flees into the Toy Shop, and one
thing I found kind of interesting here is

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:20.060
that the front window of this place, Playland
Toys shows all of these toys driving cars,

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.119
and that’s like the one thing Chucky can’t
do.

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:26.070
In all of the sequels he has to either hitch
a ride or threaten someone to drive him somewhere.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.899
There’s also a picture of Humpty Dumpty
right here next to this French duck, and that

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:32.749
could a foreshadowing about Maggie falling
down the 8th story window later.

00:01:32.749 --> 00:01:36.100
That could just be a coincidence, but I will
note that this wasn’t just a Toy Store that

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.859
they filmed in, this was built for the movie,
and also destroyed for the movie.

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:43.439
When Ray is breaking into the store, there’s
a game near the window called Fireball Island,

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:47.270
which from what I can tell is a game about
a cursed volcano, and Charles shoots in that

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.729
direction to open the door.

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:51.840
This could be a parallel to Chucky being a
cursed doll, who is eventually killed when

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.209
they shoot it in the heart.

00:01:53.209 --> 00:01:58.079
Again, those are questionably intentional,
but here’s one that definitely isn’t intentional,

00:01:58.079 --> 00:01:59.740
but I found kind of interesting anyway.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.679
When the title comes on screen, all the letters
are capitalized besides A and I, and in the

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:08.140
2019 version of Child’s Play, Chucky is
an AI, an artificial intelligence.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.430
As the dying Charles makes his way through
the store, he keeps saying he’s gotta find

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.430
somebody.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:16.110
“I’ve gotta find somebody.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.860
I’ve gotta find somebody.”

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.670
Then when he knocks over the stack of Good
Guy dolls, he look surprised, as if an idea

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.670
has just hit him.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:28.349
I think he memorized the voodoo incantation
with the intention of transferring his soul

00:02:28.349 --> 00:02:32.319
into another human in case he ever got in
trouble, but since there were no humans around,

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:36.099
he figured his best bet was to try to send
it into the doll, and by a stroke of luck,

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:37.099
it worked.

00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:40.040
He even tells John Bishop later that we was
kind of surprised that it worked.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.860
The next day, is our protagonist Andy Barclay’s
birthday.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.160
He gets up early to watch his favorite show,
Good Guys.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.220
Roll it.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.780
“No one will play with me.”

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.380
“Uh oh.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:52.740
There’s a friend in need.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Hey cheer up!”

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.000
“Who are you?”

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.140
“I am Doctor Rabbit!”

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:03.320
No, but what I actually wanted to point out
was this kid in the cartoon has a target on

00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:07.250
his chest, just as Andy becomes the target
of Chucky after learning that he is the only

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.489
one that he’ll be able to transfer his soul
into.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:12.379
Andy isn’t interested in the show though,
because he’s apparently already seen it,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.560
so he returns to the kitchen so he can continue
being a complete brat.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.560
The brand of the bread he uses for his mother’s
toast is “good stuff” which matches the

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.129
constant Good Guys branding on almost everything
he owns.

00:03:34.129 --> 00:03:37.930
I’m genuinely surprised that they didn’t
make this Good Guys mascot the villain of

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.560
the entire movie instead of the doll, he’s
way creepier.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:41.560
Look at this thing.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.192
Imagine this chasing after you in a dark alley.

00:03:44.192 --> 00:03:45.192
Would have been way better.

00:03:45.192 --> 00:03:46.819
At the end of that commercial we hear the
following:

00:03:46.819 --> 00:03:52.120
“Brought to you exclusively by Play Pals,
makers of Good Guys and other fine toys.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.310
Found in Toy Stores throughout the greater
Chicago area.”

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.469
Play Pals would later play a more prominent
role in the sequel Child’s Play 2, though

00:03:59.469 --> 00:04:03.010
there looks to be an error later in the movie
where it says Play Partners Toys on the Good

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.760
Guy box instead of Play Pals.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.760
Close enough I guess.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.480
Speaking of errors, when Andy, sees that commercial,
that the first time he’s hearing about The

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.120
Good Guy doll.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:12.489
“Wow!!”

00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:16.030
Then he goes into the other room wakes up
his Mom, then she lets him open his birthday

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.030
presents.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:18.030
“Well what do you think?”

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.989
“I want a Good Guy to go with it.”

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:21.389
“I know you do Andy--”

00:04:21.389 --> 00:04:23.330
Wait, hold up, stop it right there.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.330
No.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.330
No you didn’t know he wanted a Good Guy.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.120
He just found out about it five minutes ago
while you were asleep.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.300
Alright, let’s continue.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.430
Andy’s Mom is able to buy the doll from
a peddler and give it Andy.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:35.320
The design of the Good Guy doll is based off
of the My Buddy Doll from the 80s.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.820
“My Buddy.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:38.140
My Buddy.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:38.640
My Buddy.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.240
MY BUDDY!”

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.699
Andy’s Mom has to work late, so her friend
Maggie watches Andy that night.

00:04:46.699 --> 00:04:50.720
As she’s turning off the TV, a news report
talks about, Eddie Caputo who escaped during

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.820
a prison bus transfer on his way to court.

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:55.310
You’ll already know about this if you’ve
seen the movie multiple times, but it’s

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.810
not as obvious on a first watch.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:00.280
Eddie was Charles’s accomplice the night
before at the toy store who bailed out picking

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.930
him up in the van.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:03.930
“Eddie!

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:04.930
Eddie don’t leave me, God no!”

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.840
So Chucky goes after him later and blows up
his hideout.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.960
"WTF BOOM--"

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.280
Also, the news station is called W-DOL.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.240
You know, cause Chucky’s a doll.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.080
Chucky pushes Maggie out of the window where
she falls harder than James Charles’s career,

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.350
so Karen ends up coming home to an apartment
full of cops.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.480
"What?"

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.780
“Ms Peterson’s dead Ms Barclay.”

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:32.280
“What?’

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.660
Wait, how are you surprised by that?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:35.660
After this?

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.980
"Nothing to see, now let's move it..."

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.280
After this?

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:42.420
And after this?

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.660
“Mrs. Barclay, I’m detective Mike Norris,
homicide.”

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:50.340
So the cops clear out after he explains everything,
and the next day Karen takes her son to school…

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.610
and let’s him bring the Chucky doll with?

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:56.259
This is almost as bad as when that kid brought
his cat to school in Pet Sematary 2.

00:05:56.259 --> 00:06:00.199
Yeah, this video really took a wrong turn
if we’re talking about Pet Sematary 2 again.

00:06:00.199 --> 00:06:03.800
Andy skips school and Chucky makes him go
to Eddie’s hideout so he can get his revenge.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.620
The police find Andy and pick him up, where
they discover he believes Chucky is alive

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:09.879
and send him in for a mental evaluation.

00:06:09.879 --> 00:06:11.900
Karen is left to give Chucky a closer look.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:14.610
At the apartment, there’s a photo of a guy
in a red shirt.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:17.910
I’m guessing that’s supposed to be Andy’s
deceased father, they have the same photo

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.720
all over the house, but it’s actually just
the director of the movie, Tom Holland.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:25.220
He also makes a cameo as the voice during
that creepy commercial I mentioned earlier.--

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:29.379
Chucky tries to kill officer Norris, and is
almost successful, but Norris ends up shooting

00:06:29.379 --> 00:06:33.610
him, and Chucky discovers he’s able to feel
pain, so he hits up his pal John Bishop, the

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:36.730
voodoo doctor, to try to figure out how to
remedy the situation.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:40.280
He learns that his doll form is becoming human
and Chucky threatens him with a voodoo doll

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.650
to try to get more information.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.600
“You shouldn’t tell your customers where
you hide things like this John.”

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:51.050
Wait, so we are to believe that John made
a voodoo doll of himself?

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.270
Why?

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.270
How would that?

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.849
You know what, **** it, let’s just continue
on with this video.

00:06:55.849 --> 00:06:58.160
"AGHHHH!!!"

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.040
“So long Jonn”.

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:03.639
And so, Chucky learns he must transfer his
soul into the person who he first revealed

00:07:03.639 --> 00:07:05.930
himself to, which of course is Andy.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:09.159
So Chucky tries to break into the hospital
where the little **** is being kept and all

00:07:09.159 --> 00:07:11.220
the sudden he’s freaking massive on the
stairs.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:14.300
Look at this, it’s like that mascot I was
talking about earlier.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.340
And are we really supposed to believe that
Andy, the kid who could not even pour a bowl

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:20.990
of cereal properly, was clever enough to set
that bait with the pillow and escape when

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:22.070
Chucky came in?

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:25.139
And one more thing, why do they have this
shock device, which apparently is capable

00:07:25.139 --> 00:07:27.830
of killing a grown man, in a children’s
hospital?

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:31.099
And another thing, how does a 6 year old kid
find his way home on the streets of Chicago

00:07:31.099 --> 00:07:32.099
by himself?

00:07:32.099 --> 00:07:34.710
And it’s winter, and I’m assuming he’s
never been to this hospital before.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:35.710
Alright.

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:36.909
I’ll stop ragging on this movie now.

00:07:36.909 --> 00:07:37.909
….

00:07:37.909 --> 00:07:38.909
No I won’t.

00:07:38.909 --> 00:07:40.110
Obvious reference to Halloween.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.199
Obvious reference to The Shining.

00:07:41.199 --> 00:07:45.030
Andy’s Mom gets home and manages to trap
Chucky in the fireplace, and we actually get

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.139
a pretty cool one liner from Andy.

00:07:47.139 --> 00:07:50.470
“Andy, no please.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:54.000
We’re friends to the end, remember?”

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.640
“This is the end, friend.”

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:01.560
It isn’t.

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:03.800
They blow Chucky’s head off, he comes back.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.139
They blow his arm off.

00:08:05.139 --> 00:08:06.159
He comes back.

00:08:06.159 --> 00:08:07.389
And then finally, they figure it out!

00:08:07.389 --> 00:08:08.970
For some reason, you have to shoot it in the
heart!

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:09.970
“The heart!

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:11.289
Shoot him in the heart!”

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:14.840
Cue the Bov Jovi end credits song!

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:16.740
What?

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:17.789
No Shot Through The Heart?

00:08:17.789 --> 00:08:18.980
Are you kidding me?

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:19.980
This was the 80s!

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.160
The song came out like two years before this
movie!

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.160
It would have been perfect.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.160
Alright, whatever.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.620
Click the video on the left if you want to
see some Things You Missed in the teaser trailer

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.120
and ARG for the new Child’s Play remake.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:31.770
Next week I’m doing Child’s Play 2 and
3, and of course I’ll be doing the new movie

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:32.840
when it comes out.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.169
So, here’s what you gotta do.

00:08:34.169 --> 00:08:38.979
Subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every
week, ring that deathbell for notifications

00:08:38.979 --> 00:08:41.349
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:08:41.349 --> 00:08:43.289
Assuming we both survive.

